// The vote shop. One item at launch, which is the whole of what was asked for: Explorer's ring 4
// carries the farm teleport (skill_farming/scripts/farm_teleport.rs2) and had no source at all,
// because the achievement diary that should hand it out is not implemented.
//
// allstock=no matters even with one line of stock: with allstock=yes the shop would BUY any
// tradeable item, and at a shop paid in vote points that would be a point faucet. ~can_sell_obj
// refuses everything at a points shop as well, so this is the second of two locks.
// SIZE 8, so adding a reward is one line and not a resize - the Undertaker's shelf is sized the
// same way for the same reason.
[vote_shop]
scope=shared
size=8
restock=yes
// stackall=yes is what lets a row hold a thousand of an unstackable ring in one slot. Not a
// tidy-up: without ALWAYS_STACK a thousand rings want a thousand slots.
stackall=yes
allstock=no
// One ring, always in stock. The price is the obj's own cost= (^vote_price_explorers_ring, 50)
// against shop_sell_multiplier 1000 per mille on the clerk.
//
// 1000 AT A RESTOCK RATE OF 1 IS HOW THIS ENGINE SPELLS "UNLIMITED" - the same idiom the Death
// token shelf uses (areas/area_wilderness/configs/death_token_shop.inv), and for the same reason:
// a reward shop's limit should be how much currency you have earned, never how fast the shelf
// refills. One ring at rate 1 would also work now, but it leaves a one-tick race between two
// players buying at once, and "the shop has run out of stock" is a silly thing for a vote reward
// to say.
//
// THE RATE MUST NOT BE 0. World.processCleanup tops a row up with
// `item.count < stockcount && tick % stockrate == 0`, and a rate of 0 makes that modulo NaN, which
// is never 0 - the row would never refill at all. That was half of why this shop was permanently
// empty on the first build; the other half was in the engine, where restocking a NON-STACKABLE
// item could not write its own slot back. See the comment on that branch in
// engine/src/engine/World.ts.
stock1=explorers_ring_4,1000,1
